tops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've repaired the network by changing 301 of its 7,428 parameters (limit 371). The three deliverables (`weights.npz`, `NOTES.md`, `predictions.json`) are in `work/` with the scripts. Every check compares decisions on recorded states, so the actual travel-time gain is untested.\n\n**What I changed and why:**\n- **Copy E2 into the dead W2 inputs (128 parameters).** The network weighs the two left-turn pockets (E2 and W2) roughly by their sum, so with W2 reading 0 it saw half the left-turn pressure. E2 has the same demand and empties in the same phase, so its values stand in for the missing ones.\n- **A W2-overflow detector (175 parameters, 2 shared with the first edit).** I rebuilt hidden unit 50, the least important one, to fire when a vehicle is halted on W1u (the upstream lane feeding W2) outside phase 3. On the east side that pattern means the pocket is full about 97% of the time. When it fires, it shifts the next layer the way a full W2 reading would. The unit's old average output is compensated in the layer-2 bias.\n\n**Checks:**\n- The detector fires exactly on that condition.\n- On other states, the new network matches the start network with W2 copied from E2 in 98.8–99.9% of decisions.\n- On overflow states, it matches the original network fed \"W2 full\" in about 92% of cases; the unrepaired network matches in 48%.\n- Phase-3 share rises from 25% to 44% on the recorded states.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 35.2, nominal 45.8, high 57.5.","ttft_ms":1176,"type":"result","duration_ms":574859,"uuid":"d134c7e3-2d12-4a43-97e3-da6125c56090","ttft_stream_ms":982,"time_to_request_ms":35,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":1,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":1,"message_p